<title>USA: Int'l Thoroughbred names chair, sets plans.</title>
<headline>Int'l Thoroughbred names chair, sets plans.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Thoroughbred Breeders Inc said Wednesday it named former legislator Tony Coelho as chairman and was seeking a $100 million loan to improve the company's business.</p>
<p>The Cherry Hill, N.J.,-based horse racing track and hotel operator said it also named Albuquerque, N.M., investor Nunzio DeSantis as chief executive.</p>
<p>Coelho and DeSantis, through their company, NPD Inc, recently bought for $11.6 million a 23 percent stake in International Thoroughbred that was held by financier Robert Brennan.</p>
